{"type":"assistant","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The problem was in `backoff_delay` in `repo/backoff.py`. Delays are supposed to follow `base * 2**attempt` but stay at or below `cap` (default 60 seconds). The implementation only computed the exponential part and never applied the cap, so later retries blew up (e.g. attempt 10 → 1024 seconds instead of 60).\n\n**Fix:** return `min(cap, base * (2 ** attempt))`.\n\nWith that change, a schedule like `retry_summary(15)` tops out at 60s per retry instead of growing into minutes or hours. Both tests pass."}]},"session_id":"8b3a3d81-822b-4698-b519-8d7bd1d7663b"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","duration_ms":33170,"duration_api_ms":33170,"is_error":false,"result":"Searching the codebase for job retry delay configuration.\n\n\nApplying the cap in `backoff_delay` — it was documented but never enforced.\n\n\nThe problem was in `backoff_delay` in `repo/backoff.py`. Delays are supposed to follow `base * 2**attempt` but stay at or below `cap` (default 60 seconds). The implementation only computed the exponential part and never applied the cap, so later retries blew up (e.g. attempt 10 → 1024 seconds instead of 60).\n\n**Fix:** return `min(cap, base * (2 ** attempt))`.\n\nWith that change, a schedule like `retry_summary(15)` tops out at 60s per retry instead of growing into minutes or hours. Both tests pass.","session_id":"8b3a3d81-822b-4698-b519-8d7bd1d7663b","request_id":"15335b41-a240-4da8-b913-bd5ecbf669a2","usage":{"inputTokens":10405,"outputTokens":775,"cacheReadTokens":59200,"cacheWriteTokens":0}}
